Z||000000||Philphine||07-30-2000||12:08 AM||||<BR>kinda boring actually. maybe because i wasn't in the ramada and kind of poping in and out. also got there at the end of the show. met a few forum members who seemed nice. rain pretty much kept things down too.<P>i did get to look at a 3.4 4cam installed and ask a few questions. it seemed at the show most of the cars were people showing compleatly stock cars. there were other modded cars there but few at the main showing. saw a car with v8 licence plates but it was closed and the owner not around. same for a fiero with a northstar engine. guess i needed to hang around more. i'm not much of a hanging around type person.<P>also learned that although i like the nic on the net, saying "hello, i'm philphine" sounds kind of silly.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Guinea Pig||07-30-2000||03:31 AM||||I too went to Jeffersonville.  Over 840 miles round trip.  Got there at 12:45 p.m. Indiana time.  Left home at 4 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">o a.m. northwestern Illinois time.  Under the circunstances, I thought it turned out great.  Spoke with John Norman about his Northstar powered Fiero, listened while the other Northstar owner explained the workings of his Fiero to another inquirer.  Met a very interesting group of Canadian Fiero owners.  Enjoyed the "hot pursuit" between the Fiero "police" car and one of the speeding miscreants.  Also observed that there were several women there who presented their Fieros very well.  Noticed Old Lar there with his camera. Fiero Phil was out mixing  with the crowd.  I saw Kieth has the Great Pumpkin repaired and looking well.  I was able to finalise a parts purchase deal and was able to meet the seller.  My interest is in the 3800's.  I was able to meet and speak with a couple owners and get some ideas from them.  All in all I had a good time and a productive afternoon in the rain under the bridge.  Had to leave at 2:00 p.m.<BR>The rain was unfortunate and did hamper what is usually a very good display of imaginative customs and modifieds and well preserved stockers.  It was nice to have a bridge under which to take cover and salvage the show.  Would like to have been able to stay longer and to have arrived the 27th, but that wasn't the case.  Anyway, next year I may even have my Fiero ready to show.  My toy got broken and had to be taken back to the toy maker.  Sure would like to make the Canadian show. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||07-31-2000||10:31 AM||||Darn, I didn't get to meet you guys there. I know I also missed Old Lar and Phil. Just to much to do and SEE !!!||||reg||1
